{
  "summary": "Converts `building-on` in `contrib/guix/toolchains.scm` from an eagerly evaluated variable into a procedure called during derivation lowering. This ensures the `--build` flag uses the architecture passed via Guix's `--system` flag rather than the architecture of the host executing `guix shell`.",
  "problem": "When running Guix with `--system` on a different host architecture under emulation (for example, `--system=aarch64-linux` on an x86_64 machine), `guix shell` loads the manifest before applying `--system`. As a result, `(%current-system)` evaluates to the host's architecture at module load time, generating a mismatched `--build=x86_64-guix-linux-gnu` flag that causes `gcc-cross-sans-libc` to fail during configuration.",
